<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Posts on My Ananke Website</title><link>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/</link><description>Recent content in Posts on My Ananke Website</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 18 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>First Post</title><link>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/first-post/</link><pubDate>Tue, 18 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/first-post/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Here’s my first post.
Now I want to change something here to see if the &lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;hard reset&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; of the local branch to match the remote has gone well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;git&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;origin&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;git&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;reset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;--hard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;origin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;optional&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;git&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;clean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;-fd&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;git clean -fd&lt;/strong&gt; removes all untracked files and directories from your working directory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The listed folders (assets/, data/, i18n/, layouts/) were &lt;strong&gt;not tracked by git&lt;/strong&gt; (i.e., not part of any commit).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After this, those folders are &lt;strong&gt;deleted locally&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/images/sky_quad.png" alt="some quad sky image"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Getting to Know the Ananke Theme</title><link>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/explore-ananke/</link><pubDate>Tue, 18 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/explore-ananke/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="what-is-ananke"&gt;What is Ananke?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ananke is a popular theme for &lt;a href="https://gohugo.io"&gt;Hugo&lt;/a&gt;, designed to be fast, flexible, and easy to use. It supports a beautiful hero image, post listing grid, and is responsive by default.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://ananke-theme.netlify.app/"&gt;Ananke Theme Demo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/theNewDynamic/gohugo-theme-ananke#configuration"&gt;Theme Configuration Options&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="how-to-customize"&gt;How to Customize&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Edit the &lt;code&gt;[params]&lt;/code&gt; in your &lt;code&gt;config.toml&lt;/code&gt; file to change the hero image, subtitle, colors, and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;[&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;]
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;hero_image&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;/my-ananke-project/images/hero.jpg&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;hero_subtitle&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Learning Hugo the Fun Way!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to tweak the homepage and card layouts?&lt;br&gt;
Explore the theme’s example site in the repo:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://github.com/theNewDynamic/gohugo-theme-ananke/tree/master/exampleSite"&gt;https://github.com/theNewDynamic/gohugo-theme-ananke/tree/master/exampleSite&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Markdown Basics for Hugo</title><link>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/markdown-basics/</link><pubDate>Tue, 18 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/markdown-basics/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="what-is-markdown"&gt;What is Markdown?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Markdown is a simple, readable markup language that’s perfect for creating content for Hugo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="basic-syntax"&gt;Basic Syntax&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Headers:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;# Big Title&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;## Section&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bold/Italics:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;**bold**&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;*italic*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lists:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;- Bullet item&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Links:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;[Hugo Docs](https://gohugo.io/documentation/)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Images:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;![Example](/my-ananke-project/images/example.jpg)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="try-it-yourself"&gt;Try it Yourself!&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;## My Section Title
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Here&amp;#39;s some descriptive text about Hugo and Ananke!
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; Fast setup
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; Simple Markdown writing
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;[&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;Learn more&lt;/span&gt;](&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;https://commonmark.org/help/&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want more? &lt;a href="https://www.markdownguide.org/basic-syntax/"&gt;Markdown Guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>What is Hugo?</title><link>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/hugo-introduction/</link><pubDate>Tue, 18 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://gitana19.github.io/my-ananke-project/posts/hugo-introduction/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="hugo-static-sites-made-simple"&gt;Hugo: Static Sites Made Simple&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hugo is a blazing-fast, open source static site generator written in Go.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="key-features"&gt;Key Features&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simple content structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instant builds (great for deploying to GitHub Pages)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Powerful theming system (like Ananke!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="useful-links"&gt;Useful Links&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://gohugo.io/documentation/"&gt;Hugo Official Docs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://gohugo.io/getting-started/quick-start/"&gt;Getting Started with Hugo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Try running:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;hugo new site my-ananke-project
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;hugo server
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;to preview your site locally!&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>